{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"position","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true},{"text":" that specifies where to place a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"newly opened window relative to the screen bounds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"position"}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A scene that uses a default position for new windows."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The first time your app opens a window from a particular scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration, the system places the window at the center of the screen by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default. For scene types that support multiple simultaneous windows, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system offsets each additional window by a small amount to avoid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"completely obscuring existing windows.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can override the default placement of the first window by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applying a scene modifier that indicates where to place the window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to the screen bounds. For example, you can request that the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system place a new window in the bottom trailing corner of the screen:"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultPosition(.bottomTrailing)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The system aligns the point in the window that corresponds to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with the point in the screen that corresponds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the same unit point."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You typically use one of the predefined unit points — like"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing"},{"type":"text","text":" in the above example — but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can also use a custom unit point. For example, the following"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"modifier aligns the point that’s one quarter of the way from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leading edge of the window with the point that’s one quarter of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the way from the leading edge of the screen, while centering the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window in the y-dimension:"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".defaultPosition(UnitPoint(x: 0.25, y: 0.5))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier affects any scene type that creates windows in macOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"namely:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Window"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DocumentGroup","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Settings"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The value that you provide acts only as an initial default. During state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restoration, the system restores the window to the position that it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last occupied."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultPosition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5ScenePAAE15defaultPositionyQrAA9UnitPointVF","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"symbolKind":"method","title":"defaultPosition(_:)","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Ins